From e2d6b0b91cd9bad647f3bc42d758680cf5d91b76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jan Forst <ensonador@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:10:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] target_budget.txt: the pinned toolchain's loop counts

The static target budget failed from a stock checkout of this pin: the pinned toolchain
(jieli-linux-toolchains-20260730.1) counts the render loops differently from the compiler SLOOP 2.4/2.5
measured with, so drums_mix read +11 % and fm1_alnk0_irq +54 % over budget. Remeasured with
BUDGET_UPDATE=1 on an unpatched build and on ours: the two print identical numbers, so the change is
the compiler's, not the firmware's. The FM6 lines are the budgets SLOOP 2.4 deferred until the engine
could be measured on the target toolchain; they are static instruction counts, no audio changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tests/target_budget.txt | 25 ++++++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tests/target_budget.txt b/tests/target_budget.txt
index 1608b4e..8a917c1 100644
--- a/tests/target_budget.txt
+++ b/tests/target_budget.txt
@@ -7,18 +7,25 @@
 # SLOOP 2.4: FM6 (fm6_op_run, fm6_op_fb: the per-sample operator loops; fm6_render: the voice's output loop)
 # are in FUNCS without a budget yet: the engine was ported on a host without the pi32v2 toolchain; the
 # next ./build.sh + BUDGET_UPDATE=1 adds their lines (until then they print "no budget", not a failure).
-analog_render 638
+# fm-1-experiments: remeasured with the pinned toolchain (jieli-linux-toolchains-20260730.1). Its clang
+# counts the loops differently from SLOOP 2.5's: an unpatched checkout of this pin costs exactly these
+# numbers too, so they follow the compiler, not a change of the sound. The FM6 lines are the ones 2.4
+# deferred.
+analog_render 630
 digital_render 333
 phase_render 79
 lofi_render 128
-sample_render 126
+sample_render 130
 formant_render 314
 trio_render 341
 trio_pass 175
-drawbar_render 267
-drawbar_block 102
-grain_render 1734
-grain_block 138
-slicer_track 825
-drums_mix 6153
-fm1_alnk0_irq 174
+drawbar_render 271
+drawbar_block 103
+grain_render 1748
+grain_block 132
+slicer_track 832
+drums_mix 6811
+fm6_op_run 72
+fm6_op_fb 26
+fm6_render 362
+fm1_alnk0_irq 268
